/F1 18 Tf (Architectural Foundations of Agentic AI Systems) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
(Technical Whitepaper - Version 2.4) Tj T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf (1. Executive Summary) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
(Autonomous Agentic AI systems represent an evolutionary leap from passive language models) Tj T*
(to active decision-makers capable of perception, planning, tool usage, and memory retention.) Tj T*
(Modern agents operate via iterative reasoning loops such as ReAct \(Reasoning + Acting\),) Tj T*
(evaluating intermediate observations to navigate dynamic, non-deterministic environments.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf (2. Core Pillars of Agentic Architecture) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
(An agentic system relies upon four foundational subsystems:) Tj T*
(1. Perception and Context Processing: Ingestion of multimodal prompts, environment state, and documents.) Tj T*
(2. Planning and Decomposition: Breaking down complex objectives into directed acyclic task graphs.) Tj T*
(3. Tool Integration: Executing deterministic APIs, bash terminals, web search, and vector databases.) Tj T*
(4. Memory Systems: Short-term episodic context windows combined with long-term semantic stores.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
