/F1 18 Tf (Security, Safety, and Evaluation Metrics) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf (5. Security Vectors in Agentic AI) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
(Because agents possess tool-execution capabilities, they introduce new attack surfaces:) Tj T*
(- Indirect Prompt Injection: Malicious instructions embedded within retrieved web pages or PDFs.) Tj T*
(- Privilege Escalation: Agents inadvertently running destructive bash commands or database drops.) Tj T*
(- Data Exfiltration: Attackers tricking agents into sending proprietary context to external endpoints.) Tj T*
(Mitigation requires Sandboxed Runtimes, Tool Execution Guardrails, and Human-in-the-Loop approvals.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf (6. Evaluation Frameworks) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf
(Evaluating agent performance requires multifaceted metrics:) Tj T*
(- Task Completion Rate \(TCR\): Percentage of end-to-end tasks successfully executed without errors.) Tj T*
(- Retrieval Precision@K: Ground truth relevance of chunks surfaced during RAG operations.) Tj T*
(- Tool Call Efficiency: Ratio of necessary tool invocations versus redundant retry loops.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
